# [Project Name] — Domain Language

Shared vocabulary for this project. Agents read this file before starting any task and use its terms consistently in code, commits, and documentation.

## How to Use

- Add terms as they emerge during `/discuss`, `/create-ticket`, or `/plan` sessions.
- Keep definitions tight — one sentence max. Define what it IS, not what it does.
- Be opinionated — pick the best term, list others under _Avoid_.
- Only include terms specific to this project — no general programming concepts.
- Group terms under subheadings when natural clusters emerge.

## Language

### [Domain Area]

**[Term]**:
A one-sentence definition of what this term means in this project's context.
_Avoid_: synonym1, synonym2

**[Another Term]**:
Definition.
_Avoid_: alternative name

## Relationships

- A **[Term A]** contains many **[Term B]**s
- A **[Term B]** belongs to exactly one **[Term A]**

## Example dialogue (optional)

> **Dev:** "When a [Term A] is created, does it always have [Term B]s?"
> **Domain expert:** "No — a [Term A] starts empty. [Term B]s are added during [process name]."

## Flagged ambiguities

- "[word]" was previously used to mean both X and Y — resolved: X is a **[Term A]**, Y is a **[Term B]**.
